---
layout: layouts/base.njk

pagination:
  data: locales
  size: 1
  alias: locale

# Explicit permalink — the live URLs must survive exactly. No directory URLs.
permalink: "{{ locale.urlPrefix }}events.html"
---
{#
  The bilingual events listing.

  The year structure comes from src/_data/eventListing.js, which is a pure
  function of the records and the ONE central setting in
  content/settings/academic-year.yaml. This template renders that structure; it
  contains no year logic of its own and no hard-coded "2025/26".

  Archive disclosures use native <details>/<summary>: keyboard accessible and
  fully usable with JavaScript disabled, and the content stays in the DOM and the
  accessibility tree when collapsed, so it remains findable by in-page search.
  No ARIA is added — it would only duplicate or fight the native semantics.
#}
{%- set c = records.pages.events[locale.code] -%}
{%- set seasonShort = eventListing.current.academicYear -%}
{%- set seasonLong = seasonShort | academicYearLong -%}
{#- seasonShort/seasonLong remain for the SEO copy below; the visible listing
    reads eventListing.years and names each year for itself. -#}

<section class="page-hero hero-photo">
  <div class="hero-photo-bg" style="background-image: url('{{ records.pages.events.hero_image }}'); background-position: {{ records.pages.events.hero_image_position }};" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">{{ c.eyebrow }}</span>
    <h1>{{ c.title_lead }} <span class="fancy">{{ c.title_fancy }}</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">
      {{ c.lead }}
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{#-
  ONE SECTION PER ACADEMIC YEAR, NEWEST FIRST.

  The page used to show the configured season and fold everything older into an
  archive underneath. It now treats every year the same way: each is a
  <details> carrying its own heading, its own watermark and its own cards, and
  the configured current year is the one that opens.

  That also gives a future year somewhere to be. An event published under
  2026/27 while the site is still on 2025/26 sorts to the top and arrives
  collapsed — visible, correctly placed, and not promoted over the season that
  is actually running. Which year is current is decided by Site settings alone
  and never by the content, so a record appearing early changes nothing else.

  Still native <details>/<summary>: keyboard accessible, usable with JavaScript
  off, and the content stays in the DOM when collapsed so in-page search finds
  it. No ARIA — it would fight the native semantics.
-#}
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
{%- for year in eventListing.years %}
    <details class="event-year has-watermark"{% if year.isCurrent %} open{% endif %}>
      <summary class="event-year-summary">{{ c.season_heading | replace("{season}", year.academicYear | academicYearLong) }}</summary>
      {#- The watermark belongs to THIS year, not to the page, so two sections
          can never show one year's number over another's events. -#}
      <span class="watermark" aria-hidden="true">{{ year.academicYear }}</span>
      <div class="event-year-body">
{%- if year.records.length %}
        <div class="event-list">
{% for event in year.records %}
{%- set t_page = c %}
{% include "partials/event-card.njk" %}
{% endfor %}
        </div>
{%- else %}
        {#- The current year exists in the settings but has nothing published
            yet. Older years still show below; nothing is promoted. -#}
        <p class="lead">{{ c.empty_season | replace("{season}", year.academicYear | academicYearLong) }}</p>
{%- endif %}
      </div>
    </details>
{%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="cta-band reveal">
      <h2>{{ c.cta_heading }}</h2>
      <p>{{ c.cta_text }}</p>
      {#- Relative on purpose: from /pl/ this resolves to the Polish contact page. -#}
      <a class="btn btn-light" href="contact.html">{{ c.cta_label }} <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
